Source: dell-xps-touchpad-haptics
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Homepage: https://github.com/omacom/omarchy-pkgs/tree/master/pkgbuilds/dell-xps-touchpad-haptics
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: dell-xps-touchpad-haptics
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3
Description: Haptic feedback presets for the Dell XPS Synaptics touchpad
 Omarchy's driver for the haptic touchpad of Dell XPS 14 and 16 laptops
 (Synaptics, i2c id 06CB): a daemon that talks to the touchpad over
 hidraw and plays its click feedback at the chosen strength, a systemd
 service that runs it, a udev rule that keeps the touchpad's I2C
 controller powered, and the command dell-xps-touchpad-haptics, with
 three presets: low, mid and high.
 .
 The @DISTRO_NAME@ installer installs this package on the machines it is
 for; the desktop's menu offers the presets under Hardware.
